# Copy to .env and fill in. Vite only exposes variables that start with VITE_.
VITE_ATS_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8000
# Accounts (milestone 4): the local Supabase stack that `stack:start` runs, and its publishable key,
# a fixed development key that every local stack prints the same (`pnpm exec supabase status`).
# Leave both empty to run the editor without accounts.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_ACJWlzQHlZjBrEguHvfOxg_3BJgxAaH

# Not Vite's: scripts/corpus.ts reads a GitHub token for the corpus from its environment, never
# from this file, when gh is not logged in, as in CI. Never give either the VITE_ prefix.
# GH_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Not Vite's either: the models' keys, each one line with no spaces. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is a Claude
# key from https://platform.claude.com, whose model the label route asks first (decision 0109),
# PDF_LABEL_CLAUDE_MODEL picking it by its id, claude-haiku-5-5 when unset; SoCLaaS's model is
# asked when Claude gives no answer, or alone when this key is not set.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# PDF_LABEL_CLAUDE_MODEL=
# SOCLAAS_API_KEY is a SoCLaaS key (clsk_...) from
# https://soclaas-portal.comp.nus.edu.sg (decision 0036). The reading service's route that labels an
# imported PDF's lines, /v1/label (milestone 3 second pass, item 13; scripts/serve-label.ts in the
# dev server, functions/v1/label.ts on Pages), reads them from this file or the environment, on the
# server side alone; with neither it refuses and the page's rules read the PDF. PDF_LABEL_MODEL
# picks its model by its SoCLaaS id, qwen3.8:27b when unset. `pdf-model` (scripts/pdf-model.ts),
# run by hand on the invented sets alone, reads the keys from its environment and measures the
# model PDF_LABEL_MODEL names, Claude's for an id that starts claude-. Never give any of these the
# VITE_ prefix, which would put a key in the page.
# SOCLAAS_API_KEY=
# PDF_LABEL_MODEL=
